\newlabel{tab:generalisation}{{4.11}{103}{\textbf {Whole-well holdout on the corrected evaluation, with the truth verified against the build's own fit digest and the full held-out population scored.} The two right-hand columns carry the SAME point estimate and differ only in what they treat as the unit of generalisation. On \texttt {unseen\_combo} the gap excludes zero clustered on cell line and does not clustered on drug, which is why that row is reported as \notestablished . The \texttt {unseen\_drug} row corroborates but does not prove: its \texttt {orth}-partner gap is negative while its \texttt {opposite} gap is $+0.0379$}{table.caption.167}{}}
